,{"words":[{"surface":"திருந்து","parts":[{"text":"திருந்து","lemma":"tiruntu","gloss":"perfected"}],"gloss":"perfected"},{"surface":"வேல்","parts":[{"text":"வேல்","lemma":"vēl","gloss":"spear"}],"gloss":"spear"},{"surface":"நாகற்","parts":[{"text":"நாகற்","lemma":"nākaṉ","gloss":"Nakan"}],"gloss":"Nakan"},{"surface":"கூறினர்","parts":[{"text":"கூறினர்","lemma":"kūṟiṉar","gloss":"they spoke"}],"gloss":"they spoke"},{"surface":"பலரே","parts":[{"text":"பலரே","lemma":"palar","gloss":"many people"}],"gloss":"many people"}]}],"literal":"On this earth, because the generous ones have perished, / my begging bowl, not receiving anything, turned upside down. / When I asked, 'Who will turn it upright?', they spoke of / the warrior of the Pandyan king, who wears fine ornaments desired by Lakshmi, / who conquered many lands with tightly bound drums, / who helps with his sword when an army is needed, / who helps with his wisdom when action is needed, / who gets whatever he desires in the king's land, / with a manly mind that does not bend under a weary yoke, / the lord of Nalai of unfailing good fame, / Nakan of the perfected spear and good wars / that satisfy the hunger of vultures.","translation":"Because the generous patrons of this earth have perished, my begging bowl lay turned upside down, receiving nothing. When I asked, 'Who is there to turn it upright?', many spoke of Nakan, the lord of Nalai of unfailing good fame. He is the warrior of the Pandyan king—who wears fine ornaments desired by Lakshmi and has conquered many lands with tightly bound drums. Nakan helps with his sword when an army is needed, and with his wisdom when counsel is needed. He obtains whatever he desires in the king's country, possessing a manly heart that never bends under a weary yoke. His perfected spear in righteous wars satisfies the hunger of vultures.","modern":"இவ்வுலகில் கொடையாளிகள் இறந்துவிட்டதால், இரவலனாகிய எனது பிச்சைப் பாத்திரம் ஏதும் பெறாமல் கவிழ்ந்து கிடந்தது. 'இதை நிமிர்த்தி வைப்பவர் யார்?' என்று நான் கேட்டபோது, பலர் நாலை கிழவனான நாகனைப் பற்றிக் கூறினர். அவன், திருமகள் விரும்பும் நுட்பமான அணிகலன்களை அணிந்தவனும், முழங்கும் முரசுகளுடன் பல நாடுகளை வென்றவனுமாகிய பாண்டிய மன்னனின் சிறந்த வீரன் ஆவான். படை தேவைப்படும்போது தன் வாளாலும், அறிவுரை தேவைப்படும்போது தன் அறிவாலும் அவன் மன்னனுக்கு உதவுகிறான். மன்னனின் நாட்டில் தான் விரும்பியவற்றை எல்லாம் பெறக்கூடியவன்; நுகத்தடிக்கு அஞ்சாத காளையைப் போல தளராத ஆண்மை மிக்க நெஞ்சம் கொண்டவன்; அழியாத புகழையுடைய நாலை என்னும் ஊரின் தலைவன். பருந்துகளின் பசியைத் தீர்க்கும் நற்போர்களைச் செய்யும் திருந்திய வேலை ஏந்திய நாகனைப் பலர் என்னிடம் சுட்டிக்காட்டினர்.","explanation":"The poet, Vaṭaneṭuntattaṉār, describes his relief upon finding a true patron after a period of great despair. He uses the vivid image of a turned-down begging bowl to represent his poverty, and asks who can turn it upright. Many people direct him to Nālai Kiḻavaṉ Nākaṉ, a noble and versatile warrior of the Pandyan king. Nakan is praised for helping his king with both physical strength (his sword) and intellectual counsel (his wisdom). His resilience is compared to a bull that does not bend under a heavy yoke, and his spear in battle is so effective that it feeds the hungry vultures.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,0.8],[0.8,1.2],[1.2,1.53],[1.53,1.7],[1.7,3.1],[3.1,3.6],[3.6,4.0],[4.0,4.2],[4.2,5.4],[5.4,5.76],[5.88,6.0],[6.0,6.4],[6.4,6.9],[6.9,7.9],[7.9,8.2],[8.2,9.0],[9.0,9.1],[9.1,9.8],[9.8,9.8],[9.8,10.9],[10.9,11.2],[11.2,12.2],[12.2,12.7],[12.7,13.0],[13.0,13.2],[13.2,13.89],[13.89,14.4],[14.4,14.8],[14.8,15.0],[15.0,16.3],[16.3,16.5],[16.5,17.0],[17.0,17.2],[18.49,19.02],[19.02,19.42],[19.42,20.12],[20.12,20.52],[20.52,20.52],[20.52,21.62],[21.62,21.82],[21.82,22.12],[22.12,23.52],[23.52,23.92],[23.92,24.52],[24.52,24.52],[24.52,24.52],[24.52,26.32],[26.32,26.42]],"female":[[0.0,0.7],[0.7,0.8],[0.8,1.3],[1.3,1.57],[1.57,1.7],[1.7,3.2],[3.2,3.8],[3.8,4.2],[4.2,4.4],[4.4,6.78],[6.78,6.78],[6.78,6.78],[6.78,6.78],[6.78,7.5],[7.5,8.6],[8.6,8.8],[8.8,9.7],[9.7,9.8],[9.8,10.5],[10.5,11.2],[11.2,11.3],[11.3,11.9],[11.9,12.59],[12.59,13.7],[13.7,13.9],[13.9,14.1],[14.1,14.96],[14.96,15.6],[15.6,16.1],[16.1,16.3],[16.3,18.1],[18.1,18.16],[18.16,18.3],[18.3,18.6],[19.93,20.46],[20.46,20.86],[20.86,21.66],[21.66,22.38],[22.38,23.06],[23.06,23.56],[23.56,23.76],[23.76,24.16],[24.16,25.66],[25.66,26.16],[26.16,26.76],[26.76,26.76],[26.76,26.76],[26.76,28.66],[28.66,28.86]]},"sync":[[["ஞாலம்","world"]],[["மீமிசை","upon"]],[["வள்ளியோர்","generous people"]],[["மாய்ந்து","having perished"]],[["மாய்ந்து","having perished"],["என","as"]],[["ஏலாது","not receiving"]],[["கவிழ்ந்த","turned upside down"],["என்","my"]],[["இரவல்","begging"]],[["மண்டை","bowl"]],[["மலர்ப்போர்","those who turn upright"]],[["யார்","who"]],[["என","saying"]],[["வினவலின்","because of asking"]],[["மலைந்தோர்","those who fought"]],[["விசி","tightly bound"],["பிணி","fastened"]],[["முரசமொடு","with the drum"]],[["மண்","land"],["பல","many"]],[["தந்த","given"]],[["திரு","beauty"],["வீழ்","desired"]],[["நுண்","fine"],["பூண்","ornaments"]],[["பாண்டியன்","Pandyan king"]],[["மறவன்","warrior"]],[["படை","army"]],[["வேண்டுவழி","wherever needed"]],[["வாள்","sword"]],[["உதவியும்","and helping"]],[["வினை","action"]],[["வேண்டுவழி","wherever needed"]],[["அறிவு","wisdom"]],[["உதவியும்","and helping"]],[["வேண்டுப","things desired"]],[["வேண்டுப","things desired"]],[["வேந்தன்","king"]],[["தேஎத்து","of the country"]],[["அசை","weary"],["நுகம்","yoke"]],[["படாஅ","not yielding"]],[["ஆண்","manly"],["தகை","quality"]],[["உள்ளத்து","of the mind"]],[["தோலா","unfailing"]],[["நல்","good"],["இசை","fame"]],[["நாலை","Nalai"]],[["கிழவன்","lord"]],[["பருந்து","kite"],["பசி","hunger"]],[["தீர்க்கும்","satisfying"]],[["நல்","good"],["போர்த்","war"]],[["திருந்து","perfected"],["வேல்","spear"]],[["நாகற்","Nakan"]],[["கூறினர்","they spoke"]],[["பலரே","many people"]]]}